We can create ops with device inputs:
import torch
from torch import Tensor

@torch.library.custom_op("mylib::foo", mutates_args={})
def foo(x: Tensor, y: torch.device) -> Tensor:
    return x.clone().to(y)
However we can't give them a default value:
# Case 1: string device
import torch
from torch import Tensor

@torch.library.custom_op("mylib::foo", mutates_args={})
def foo(x: Tensor, y: torch.device = "cpu") -> Tensor:
    return x.clone().to(y)
# case 2: device object
import torch
from torch import Tensor

@torch.library.custom_op("mylib::foo", mutates_args={})
def foo(x: Tensor, y: torch.device = torch.device("cpu:0")) -> Tensor:
    return x.clone().to(y)
The goal is to make these two cases work.
